  "caption": "Quinn joined the local footy team: a sprint late in the game, a hamstring that tapped out, and an old ankle sprain that never quite got its rehab finished.\n\nA previous injury is one of the biggest predictors of the next one, and sudden load jumps or sprinting while tired can add to the risk.\n\nWhat can help: Nordic hamstring curls kept up all season, a structured warm-up with running, strength, balance and landing drills, neck and shoulder strength for tacklers, and finishing rehab properly before full-speed running.\n\nA suspected concussion needs immediate medical assessment, and so does a possible neck injury or not being able to bear weight. Follow your club's return-to-play protocols.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
